The Location extension draws its map of the world from land outlines it carries
with it, taken from Natural Earth 4.1.0 "ne_110m_land" (physical, 1:110m):

  https://naciscdn.org/naturalearth/110m/physical/ne_110m_land.zip
  zip sha256 1926c621afd6ac67c3f36639bb1236134a48d82226dc675d3e3df53d02d2a3de
  ne_110m_land.shp sha256 8689e6932b8e370e2ca4587cf3ba21e460b1235db37b6ed3c172c35b4a6088de

Natural Earth's vector map data is in the public domain: no permission is
needed to use it, and crediting the authors is unnecessary. The outlines are
reduced (successive points on one line dropped, coordinates to a hundredth of a
degree) and written as wasm/src/world/land.txt; tools/world-data.py regenerates
that file from the shapefile above. The regional overlay uses Natural Earth's
ne_50m_admin_0_boundary_lines_land, ne_10m_roads and ne_10m_populated_places_simple
from https://naturalearth.s3.amazonaws.com/ (50m_cultural and 10m_cultural).
tools/atlas-data.py verifies each archive's SHA-256 and generates the grid
index and city records in wasm/src/world. No map view is fetched or reported.
tools/borders.py builds regional and globe simplifications of those same 50m
land boundaries, keeping their full detail for close views.

Offline street extracts for Bucharest and Monaco: © OpenStreetMap contributors,
https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright . The derived street databases
(bucharest.bin and monaco.bin) are available under ODbL 1.0:
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/ . Source extracts are from
Geofabrik (Europe: Romania and Monaco); tools/streets-data.py records source
checksums, selection bounds and the complete transformation. Natural Earth's
public-domain 50m country label positions and land areas are separate from the
OSM data; tools/countries.py generates them from ne_50m_admin_0_countries.
